{% comment %}
  The default document template.

  Most pages here write their own opening — a stage or a heading block at the
  top of the region — so the template adds no furniture and the blocks run
  from the first pixel. A concept that says `seo.templateH1` is telling us the
  opposite: its documents expect the template to supply the heading, and their
  regions start straight in on the body copy. That flag is what the SEO check
  already reads to decide whether a missing H1 in the content is a fault, so
  it is the same promise, kept here.
{% endcomment %}
{% if concept.seo.templateH1 %}
  <header class="wb-section pad-compact">
    <div class="container w-normal doc-head">
      <h1 class="doc-title"{{ 'doc.title' | wbf }}>{{ doc.title | escape }}</h1>
      {% if fields.lede %}<p class="doc-lede"{{ 'lede' | wbf }}>{{ fields.lede | escape }}</p>{% endif %}
    </div>
  </header>
{% endif %}
{% region 'content' %}
